Release	Format GitHub release notes	2026-11-06T22:44:38.2691005Z {"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/releases/437136595","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/releases/437136595/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/releases/437136595/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/releases/tag/js-v0.27.1","id":437136595,"author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOQYTy3M4aDizT","tag_name":"js-v0.27.1","target_commitish":"main","name":"[js] 0.27.1","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-06T22:41:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T22:44:38Z","published_at":"2026-11-06T22:44:34Z","assets":[],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/tarball/js-v0.27.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/zipball/js-v0.27.1","body":"fix: sync reliability fixes for existing tools, the session loop, providers and MCP from upstream OpenCode (#335)\n\n- `edit` and `write` serialize changes to the same file, so parallel edits no\nlonger overwrite each other (upstream #4388, #23483).\n- `edit` no longer replaces unrelated code through loose fuzzy matching, and\nan empty `oldString` no longer overwrites an existing file (upstream #30932).\n- `edit` keeps CRLF, mixed line endings and a UTF-8 BOM; `write` keeps the\nBOM (upstream #9443, #53166, #23797).\n- `replaceAll` inserts `$&`, `$1` and similar text literally.\n- The \"modified since read\" check compares file mtime and size instead of\nclocks, and treats equivalent paths as one file (upstream #17835, #20367).\n- `edit` works right after `write`, and both return a short confirmation.\n- `read` resolves relative paths against the session directory, caps output\nat 50 KB and 2000 lines, handles CRLF files, directories and file names\nwith macOS narrow no-break spaces or curly quotes, and samples only 4 KB\nfor the binary check.\n- `grep` keeps matches when some paths are unreadable (rg exit 2), searches\nhidden files except `.git`, honours aborts, times out after 30 s, and\nreports invalid regexes and missing paths clearly.\n- `glob` and `ls` no longer hang after their 100-result limit, stop rg on\nabort, do not follow symlinked directories, and ignore a user ripgrep\nconfig.\n- `bash` runs commands in `$SHELL` or bash instead of `/bin/sh`, keeps the\nend of long output (where errors are), never splits UTF-8 characters,\nbounds the live metadata preview, frees parser trees, and asks for\npermission for write redirects in read-only/plan modes.\n- `webfetch`, `websearch` and `codesearch` enforce the 5 MB limit while\nstreaming, time out with a clear message, retry Cloudflare challenges with\nan honest user agent, accept plain JSON or SSE replies from Exa, and pass\n`EXA_API_KEY` when set; `webfetch` defaults to markdown.\n- Tools no longer stack a new execute wrapper on every init, and `task`\nalways unsubscribes from child-session events.\n- A prompt that exceeds the context window (400 \"prompt is too long\", 413,\nmid-stream `context_length_exceeded`) compacts the session and carries on\ninstead of ending it; a second overflow stops with a clear error\n(upstream #6480, #14707).\n- Tool calls reported with finish reason `stop` still get their results sent\nback to the model (upstream #14973).\n- Retryable 5xx stream errors, plain-text rate limits, Vertex\n`RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`, OpenAI item 404s and truncated gzip bodies are\nretried; retry delays never exceed the `setTimeout` limit; API errors\ninclude the body's message.\n- A `retry-after` longer than the retry timeout now stops the turn instead of\nstarting another step, and retry-only errors can be saved on a message.\n- Interrupted tools keep their start time and partial output and are marked\n`interrupted`; non-object tool input is stored as `{ value }`; tool events\nthat arrive without `tool-input-start` are kept.\n- Lone UTF-16 surrogates, empty Anthropic/Bedrock parts and empty user\nmessages are no longer sent; provider signatures and reasoning from another\nmodel are not replayed; prompt caching merges provider options deeply and\nuses Bedrock's cache-point format; Moonshot/Kimi tool schemas are fixed.\n- Reasoning tokens are no longer charged twice, and the Anthropic thinking\nbudget is kept within the model's output limit.\n- MCP: connect and `tools/list` time out, list pagination is bounded,\nservers are listed in parallel, failed clients are closed and reported as\n`failed` (also for invalid URLs), servers without tools stay connected,\nresults without `content` are normalized, a timed-out call is really\naborted, per-tool timeouts work for server names with `_`, the connect\ntimeout is no longer `NaN`, and dispose stops grandchild processes.\n- `cancel()` rejects queued callers with an `AbortError`.\n- Memory: the SSE usage map is bounded, the usage tee branch is always read to\nthe end, retried 5xx/429 bodies are cancelled, retry sleeps and grep/bash\ndrop their abort listeners, `withTimeout` clears its timer on rejection,\ndisposed instances leave the cache, cancelled turns reject their pending\npermission asks, and deleting a session drops its file read stamps.\n- Continuous and single-shot modes no longer wait forever for `session.idle`\nwhen a prompt fails before its loop starts.\n- MCP servers accept `connect_timeout`; `timeout` keeps its previous meaning\n(listing tools). Credentials in MCP and provider URLs are masked in verbose\nlogs.\n- The default model and default compaction model are now\n`kilo/nemotron-3-ultra-free` (1M context), and the default compaction\ncascade is `(kilo/nemotron-3-ultra-free kilo/nemotron-3.5-lightning-free same)`,\nbecause Kilo withdrew Nemotron 3 Super. `kilo/nemotron-3-super-free` (and the\nbare `nemotron-3-super-free`) stays accepted as a deprecated alias that runs\non `kilo/nemotron-3-ultra-free` and logs one warning naming the\nreplacement. The free-model drift check skips deprecated aliases and\nrequires every alias target to be a built-in model.\n- Git worktrees and submodules no longer crash the CLI: the project id cache\nwas written to `.git/opencode` while `.git` is a file there, and the\nunhandled ENOTDIR rejection ended the process. The id is now cached in the\ncommon git directory (as upstream does), and a failed cache write is only\nlogged.\n- npm dependencies are refreshed to their latest releases (the `ai` SDK and\nevery `@ai-sdk/*` provider, `@agentclientprotocol/sdk`,\n`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `@opencode-ai/sdk`, `@opentui/*` 0.8,\n`command-stream`, `hono`, `remeda`, `google-auth-library`, `glob` 14,\n`minimatch` 11 and the rest). `solid-js` is no longer pinned and the\nobsolete `seroval` override is dropped. `lino-arguments` stays on 0.3.x:\n0.4.0 throws \"Ambiguous environment aliases\" at startup when both spellings\nof a variable are set (for example `http_proxy` and `HTTP_PROXY`).\n\nBackward compatibility: every user-visible change can be reverted with an\noption (each also has a `LINK_ASSISTANT_AGENT_*` env var): `--bash-shell legacy`,\n`--legacy-tool-output`, `--legacy-edit-matching`, `--glob-follow-symlinks`,\n`--no-grep-hidden`, `--grep-timeout-ms 0`, `--read-max-lines 0`,\n`--read-max-bytes 0`, `--legacy-error-names`, `--legacy-token-usage`,\n`--legacy-loop-exit` and `--mcp-connect-timeout 0`.\n\n**Related Pull Request:** #339\n\n---\n\n[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/badge/npm-0.27.1-blue.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@link-assistant/agent/v/0.27.1)"}✅ Formatted release notes for v0.27.1
